commit db9981f7acb1d3f24d50092898c49b277b163329
Author: missingbulb <73882448+missingbulb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 6 10:00:40 2026 +0300

    Keep Claudinite's own bookkeeping inside .claudinite/: mount attributes, no README row (#1754)

    * Move Claudinite's git attributes into the mount's own .gitattributes

    Every line the corpus planted in a member's root .gitattributes was about a
    file inside .claudinite/ — the two generated indexes, the shared subtree, the
    usage fold. git reads a .gitattributes in any directory with its patterns
    relative to that directory, so the mount now carries its own and the member's
    root file stays the repo's own.

    The converged file is constant: `*GENERATED* merge=ours` subsumes the three
    named merge lines and covers whatever the mount generates next, so it never
    grows a line per artifact. The converge takes back the four lines it used to
    plant at the root, and removes a root file that held nothing else.

    generated-merge-driver splits its coverage to match, asserting nothing about
    paths under .claudinite/ until the engine that writes their attributes file
    has arrived — packs and the engine deliver on separate cadences.

    Closes #1748

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01V4vTR8vxAV9DpRNhKrWSqo

    * Stop writing a pack-badge row into a member's README

    A repo's front page is the repo's. The row was seeded at adoption and never
    converged after, so nothing here maintained it — but adoption still wrote
    Claudinite's own bookkeeping into the one file a member's readers open first.

    Removes the mechanism whole: the row's converge and its entry derivation, the
    marker constants, bootstrap's --badges flag, the adopt-pack refresh step and
    this repo's own row. The badge artwork stays where it is read — each pack's
    README and the dashboard — and a member that already carries a row keeps it,
    since the markers make it removable by hand.

===
